Error [E0121]: `item` was consumed by an escaping lambda, so it can't be used here
  --> lambda_escape_no_take.jet:14:10
    |
 14 |     sink(item)
    |          ^^^^
  --> lambda_escape_no_take.jet:11:10
    |
 11 |     f :: () -> {
    |          ^^^^^^^ `item` moved to an escaping lambda here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `item` after the move, or give an escaping lambda a copy with `~item` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
